    passage: Act 16:1-5
    entry: PAUL
    note: Visits Lystra; circumcises Timothy
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 16:6
    entry: PAUL
    note: Goes through Phrygia and Galatia; is forbidden by the Holy Spirit  to preach in Asia; visits Mysia; attempts to go to Bithynia, but is restrained by  the Spirit
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 16:7
    entry: PAUL
    note: Goes through Phrygia and Galatia; is forbidden by the Holy Spirit  to preach in Asia; visits Mysia; attempts to go to Bithynia, but is restrained by  the Spirit
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 16:8-10
    entry: PAUL
    note: Goes to Troas, where he has a vision of a man saying, &#8220;Come over  into Macedonia, and help us; &#8220;immediately proceeds to Macedonia
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 16:11-15
    entry: PAUL
    note: Visits Samothracia and Neapolis; comes to Philippi, the chief  city of Macedonia; visits a place of prayer at the side of the river; preaches the  word; the merchant, Lydia, from Thyatira, is converted and immersed
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 16:16-18
    entry: PAUL
    note: Reproves the soothsayer; causes the evil spirit to come out of  the girl who practises divination
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 16:19-34
    entry: PAUL
    note: Persecuted, beaten, and cast into prison with Silas; sings songs  of praise in the prison; an earthquake shakes the prison; he preaches to the alarmed  jailer, who believes, and is immersed along with his household
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 16:35-39
    entry: PAUL
    note: Is released by the civil authorities on the grounds of his being  a Roman citizen
END ITEM

