    passage: Act 17:1-4
    entry: PAUL
    note: Visits Amphipolis, Apollonia, and Thessalonica; preaches in the  synagogue
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 17:5-9
    entry: PAUL
    note: Is persecuted
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: 2Th 1:1-4
    entry: PAUL
    note: Is persecuted
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 17:10-12
    entry: PAUL
    note: Escapes to Berea by night; preaches in the synagogue; many honorable  women and several men believe
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 17:13-15
    entry: PAUL
    note: Persecuted by the Jews who come from Thessalonica; is escorted  by some of the brethren to Athens
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 17:16-34
    entry: PAUL
    note: Debates on Mars' Hill (at the meeting of the Areopagus Council)  with Greeks
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 18:1-3
    entry: PAUL
    note: Visits Corinth; lives with Aquila and his wife, Priscilla (Prisca),  who were tentmakers; joins in their trade
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 18:4-11
    entry: PAUL
    note: Reasons in the synagogue every Sabbath; is rejected by the Jews; turns to the Gentiles; makes his home with Justus; continues there for eighteen  months, teaching the word of God
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 18:12-18
    entry: PAUL
    note: Persecuted by Jews, drawn before the deputy, charged with wicked  lewdness; accusation dismissed; takes his leave after many days, and sails to Syria,  accompanied by Aquila and Priscilla
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 18:18-23
    entry: PAUL
    note: Visits Ephesus, where he leaves Aquila and Priscilla; enters  into a synagogue, where he reasons with the Jews; starts on his return trip to Jerusalem; visits Caesarea; crosses over the country of Galatia and Phrygia, strengthening  the disciples
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 19:12
    entry: PAUL
    note: Returns to Ephesus; immerses in the name of the Lord Jesus, and  lays his hands upon the disciples, who are baptized with the Holy Spirit; preaches  in the synagogue; remains in Ephesus for two years; heals the sick people
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 19:13-20
    entry: PAUL
    note: Rebukes the exorcists; casts an evil spirit out of a man, and  many believe, bringing their evil books of sorcery to be burned
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: 1Co 16:8
    entry: PAUL
    note: Rebukes the exorcists; casts an evil spirit out of a man, and  many believe, bringing their evil books of sorcery to be burned
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: 1Co 16:9
    entry: PAUL
    note: Rebukes the exorcists; casts an evil spirit out of a man, and  many believe, bringing their evil books of sorcery to be burned
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 19:21
    entry: PAUL
    note: Sends Timothy and Erastus into Macedonia, but he himself remains  in Asia for a period of time
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 19:22
    entry: PAUL
    note: Sends Timothy and Erastus into Macedonia, but he himself remains  in Asia for a period of time
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 19:23-41
    entry: PAUL
    note: The spread of the gospel through his preaching interferes with  the makers of idols; he is persecuted, and a great uproar of the city is created; the town clerk appeases the people; dismisses the accusation against Paul, and disperses  the people
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: 2Co 1:8
    entry: PAUL
    note: The spread of the gospel through his preaching interferes with  the makers of idols; he is persecuted, and a great uproar of the city is created; the town clerk appeases the people; dismisses the accusation against Paul, and disperses  the people
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: 2Ti 4:14
    entry: PAUL
    note: The spread of the gospel through his preaching interferes with  the makers of idols; he is persecuted, and a great uproar of the city is created; the town clerk appeases the people; dismisses the accusation against Paul, and disperses  the people
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 20:1-6
    entry: PAUL
    note: Proceeds to Macedonia after strengthening the congregations in  that region; comes into Greece and lives for three months; returns through Macedonia,  accompanied by Sopater, Aristarchus, Secundus, Gaius, Timothy, Tychicus, and Trophimus
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 20:6-12
    entry: PAUL
    note: Visits Troas; preaches until daybreak; restores to life the young  man (Eutychus) who fell from the window
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 20:13-16
    entry: PAUL
    note: Visits Assos, Mitylene, Chios, Samos, Trogyllium, and Miletus,  hastening to Jerusalem, to be there by Pentecost day
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 20:17-21
    entry: PAUL
    note: Sends for the elders of the congregation of Ephesus; relates  to them how he had preached in Asia and his temptations and afflictions, urging  repentance toward God
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 20:22-38
    entry: PAUL
    note: Declares he was going bound in spirit to Jerusalem; exhorts them  to take heed to themselves and the flock over whom the Holy Spirit had made them  overseers; kneels down, prays, and leaves
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 21:1-3
    entry: PAUL
    note: Visits Coos, Rhodes, and Patara; boards a ship bound for Tyre
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 21:4-7
    entry: PAUL
    note: Waits at Tyre for seven days; is brought on his way by the disciples  to the outskirts of the city; kneels down and prays; boards the ship; comes to Ptolemais; greets the brethren, and stays for one day
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 21:8-15
    entry: PAUL
    note: Departs for Caesarea; enters the house of Philip the evangelist; is admonished by the prophet Agabus not to go to Jerusalem; nevertheless, he proceeds  to Jerusalem
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 21:17-25
    entry: PAUL
    note: Is received by the brethren gladly; talks about the things that  had been done among the Gentiles through his ministry
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 21:26-33
    entry: PAUL
    note: Enters the temple courtyard; the people are stirred up against  him by some Jews from Asia; an uproar is created; he is thrust out of the temple  area; the commander of the Roman garrison intervenes and arrests him
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 21:33-40
    entry: PAUL
    note: His defense
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 22:1-21
    entry: PAUL
    note: His defense
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 22:24-30
    entry: PAUL
    note: Is confined in the fortress
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 22:30
    entry: PAUL
    note: Is brought before the Sanhedrin; his defense
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 23:1-5
    entry: PAUL
    note: Is brought before the Sanhedrin; his defense
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 23:10
    entry: PAUL
    note: Is returned to the fortress
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 23:11
    entry: PAUL
    note: Is encouraged by a vision from God, promising him that he will  give testimony in Rome
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 23:12-15
    entry: PAUL
    note: Jewish leaders conspire against his life
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 23:16-22
    entry: PAUL
    note: This plan is thwarted by his nephew
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 23:23-33
    entry: PAUL
    note: Is escorted to Caesarea by a military guard
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 23:35
    entry: PAUL
    note: Is confined in Herod's Judgment Hall in Caesarea
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 24
    entry: PAUL
    note: His trial before Governor Felix
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 24:27
    entry: PAUL
    note: Remains in custody for two years
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 25:1-12
    entry: PAUL
    note: His trial before Governor Festus
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 25:10-12
    entry: PAUL
    note: Appeals to be heard by Caesar
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    entry: PAUL
    note: His examination before Herod Agrippa II Ac 25:13-27; 26
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 27:1-5
    entry: PAUL
    note: Is taken to Rome in the custody of Julius, a centurion, and a  detachment of soldiers; boards a ship, accompanied by other prisoners, and sails  by way of the coasts of Asia; stops at Sidon, and at Myra
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 27:6-8
    entry: PAUL
    note: Transferred to a ship of Alexandria; sails by way of Cnidus,  Crete, Salamis, and the Fair Havens
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 27:9-13
    entry: PAUL
    note: Predicts misfortune to the ship; his counsel not heeded, and  the voyage resumes
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 27:14-44
    entry: PAUL
    note: The ship encounters a storm; Paul encourages and comforts the  officers and crew; the soldiers advise putting the prisoners to death; the centurion  interferes, and all on board (consisting of two-hundred and seventy-six persons)  survive
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 27:14-44
    entry: PAUL
    note: The ship is wrecked, and all on board take refuge on the island  of Melita (Malta)
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 28:1
    entry: PAUL
    note: Kind treatment by the inhabitants of the island
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 28:2
    entry: PAUL
    note: Kind treatment by the inhabitants of the island
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 28:3-6
    entry: PAUL
    note: Is bitten by a viper and miraculously unharmed
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 28:7-10
    entry: PAUL
    note: Heals the ruler's father and others
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 28:11-13
    entry: PAUL
    note: Is delayed in Melita (Malta) for three months; proceeds on the  voyage; delays at Syracuse; sails by Rhegium and Puteoli
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 28:14-16
    entry: PAUL
    note: Meets some brethren who accompany him to Rome from Appii Forum; arrives at Rome; is delivered to the captain of the guard; is permitted to live  by himself in custody of a soldier
END ITEM

ITEM @nave1905
    passage: Act 28:17-29
    entry: PAUL
    note: Summons the local Jewish leadership; states his position; is  kindly received; expounds the gospel; testifies to the kingdom of heaven
END ITEM

